            'grand-theft-auto-v' => ['long_description' => "Grand Theft Auto V tells a crime story through three protagonists: Michael, Franklin, and Trevor. Their separate lives converge around a series of risky jobs in Los Santos and the surrounding Blaine County, where ambition and old loyalties create complications.\n\nPlayers can move between the characters during much of the story, seeing events from different perspectives. The open world also offers optional activities and side stories alongside the missions. This listing is for the console platform and region shown above; its digital key is a demo item and is not redeemable. Grand Theft Auto V tells a crime story through three protagonists: Michael, Franklin, and Trevor. Their separate lives converge around a series of risky jobs in Los Santos and the surrounding Blaine County, where ambition and old loyalties create complications.\n\nPlayers can move between the characters during much of the story, seeing events from different perspectives. The open world also offers optional activities and side stories alongside the missions. This listing is for the console platform and region shown above; its digital key is a demo item and is not redeemable.  ", 'metadata' => ['developer' => 'Rockstar North', 'publisher' => 'Rockstar Games']],
            'hades' => ['long_description' => "Hades casts you as Zagreus, prince of the Underworld, making repeated attempts to reach the surface and escape his father’s realm. Each run passes through changing rooms and encounters, while conversations with the gods and residents of the House of Hades continue between attempts.\n\nWeapons, upgrades, and boons can combine in different ways, so a run’s tactics shift with the tools offered. Defeat is part of the structure: returning to the House advances character relationships and story threads rather than simply resetting progress.", 'metadata' => ['developer' => 'Supergiant Games', 'publisher' => 'Supergiant Games']],
            'stardew-valley' => ['long_description' => "Stardew Valley begins when you leave an office job to care for an inherited farm in Pelican Town. The farm can be developed at your own pace through planting, raising animals, crafting, and restoring parts of the valley. Each season changes what can grow and what the town’s residents are doing.\n\nTime can also be spent fishing, mining, cooking, and building friendships. There is no single required way to organize a day: you decide which parts of rural life to focus on and how to balance the farm with the surrounding community.", 'metadata' => ['developer' => 'ConcernedApe', 'publisher' => 'ConcernedApe']],
            'terraria' => ['long_description' => "Terraria opens with a small patch of land and a world that can be dug into, built upon, and explored. Gathering materials leads to tools, shelter, and equipment, while caves and distant biomes reveal new resources and dangers. The world is generated for each playthrough, so routes and discoveries vary.\n\nProgress comes from preparing for tougher encounters and expanding what you can craft. Building and exploration are equally central: players can shape large structures, search underground, and uncover bosses and events as their character becomes stronger. Terraria opens with a small patch of land and a world that can be dug into, built upon, and explored. Gathering materials leads to tools, shelter, and equipment, while caves and distant biomes reveal new resources and dangers. The world is generated for each playthrough, so routes and discoveries vary.\n\nProgress comes from preparing for tougher encounters and expanding what you can craft. Building and exploration are equally central: players can shape large structures, search underground, and uncover bosses and events as their character becomes stronger.", 'metadata' => ['developer' => 'Re-Logic', 'publisher' => 'Re-Logic']],
            'civilization-vi' => ['long_description' => "Civilization VI is a turn-based strategy game about guiding a society from its earliest settlements into a lasting civilization. Cities expand across the map, while technology, civic development, diplomacy, trade, and military planning all compete for attention. Terrain and neighboring powers influence how each new empire develops.\n\nLeaders and civilizations bring distinct abilities, and different victory paths reward different long-term plans. The pace is deliberate: decisions about where to settle, what to research, and how to respond to rivals shape the map over many turns.", 'metadata' => ['developer' => 'Firaxis Games', 'publisher' => '2K']],
            'no-mans-sky' => ['long_description' => "No Man’s Sky is a science-fiction exploration and survival game set across a procedurally generated universe. Players travel between planets, scan unfamiliar life and landscapes, gather materials, and improve the equipment and ships needed to go farther.\n\nThe journey can focus on discovery, trading, building, or survival. A central mystery provides direction, while the wider universe leaves room to chart systems and return to places that matter to you. The listing is a demo marketplace item; it does not provide a redeemable game key.", 'metadata' => ['developer' => 'Hello Games', 'publisher' => 'Hello Games']],
            'mass-effect-legendary-edition' => ['long_description' => "Mass Effect Legendary Edition brings together the single-player story arcs of the original Mass Effect trilogy, with the base games and their released single-player expansions assembled in one collection. Commander Shepard’s campaign follows a growing crew as a threat to the galaxy becomes harder to ignore.\n\nChoices carry across the trilogy, shaping relationships and later events. Combat and presentation have been updated for the collection, with the first game receiving the most extensive gameplay and visual refinements. The experience remains centered on its connected narrative and the companions who travel with Shepard.", 'metadata' => ['developer' => 'BioWare', 'publisher' => 'Electronic Arts']],
            'hollow-knight' => ['long_description' => "Hollow Knight sends a small wandering knight into Hallownest, a once-prosperous kingdom now left in ruins. Interconnected caverns and settlements reveal new paths as you gain abilities, meet inhabitants, and uncover why the kingdom fell.\n\nCombat is precise and deliberately challenging, with enemies and bosses requiring attention to movement and timing. Charms let you adjust your approach, while optional routes and hidden rooms reward returning to earlier areas with new tools.", 'metadata' => ['developer' => 'Team Cherry', 'publisher' => 'Team Cherry']],
            'god-of-war' => ['long_description' => "God of War follows Kratos and his son Atreus on a journey through the realms of Norse mythology. A personal promise gives their travels direction, but the people and gods they encounter complicate the path. The story places their changing relationship alongside the dangers of the world.\n\nCombat centers on Kratos’s Leviathan Axe, close-range attacks, and Atreus’s support. Exploration branches into side paths and puzzles, with equipment and abilities offering ways to develop the pair’s combat style. This console listing does not use PC system requirements.", 'metadata' => ['developer' => 'Santa Monica Studio', 'publisher' => 'PlayStation Publishing LLC']],
            'hogwarts-legacy' => ['long_description' => "Hogwarts Legacy is set in the Wizarding World during the late 1800s. You play a new Hogwarts student who can perceive and use an unusual form of ancient magic, becoming involved in a conflict that reaches beyond the school. Classes, companions, and excursions introduce different parts of the wider setting.\n\nThe school and surrounding region can be explored between story missions. Spell combinations, equipment, and character talents shape combat, while optional activities provide a change of pace from the main storyline.", 'metadata' => ['developer' => 'Avalanche Software', 'publisher' => 'Warner Bros. Games']],
            'sekiro-shadows-die-twice' => ['long_description' => "Sekiro: Shadows Die Twice follows a shinobi tasked with protecting a young lord in a war-torn version of Sengoku-era Japan. After a devastating defeat, the shinobi returns with a prosthetic arm and a chance to confront the forces pursuing his charge.\n\nCombat rewards close engagement: deflecting attacks and breaking an opponent’s posture are as important as dealing damage. The prosthetic can be fitted with tools for different situations, and stealth and traversal help you approach encounters on your own terms.", 'metadata' => ['developer' => 'FromSoftware', 'publisher' => 'Activision']],
            'resident-evil-4' => ['long_description' => "Resident Evil 4 follows agent Leon S. Kennedy on a mission to find the U.S. president’s kidnapped daughter in a remote European region. The search turns into a fight to survive against hostile locals and a threat that goes beyond a conventional rescue operation.\n\nThe reimagined game keeps the focus on tense exploration, resource decisions, and combat while rebuilding the original adventure for modern systems. Ammunition and healing supplies are limited enough that preparation and accuracy matter throughout the journey.", 'metadata' => ['developer' => 'Capcom', 'publisher' => 'Capcom']],
            'subnautica' => ['long_description' => "Subnautica places a stranded survivor beneath the surface of an alien ocean. With limited supplies, you explore reefs, caves, and deeper regions, collecting materials to craft equipment, vehicles, and habitats. Each descent expands what you can reach while increasing the risks.\n\nThe ocean’s ecosystems and scattered evidence gradually reveal the story behind the crash. Exploration is self-directed, but oxygen, food, and the capabilities of your gear shape how long each expedition can last.", 'metadata' => ['developer' => 'Unknown Worlds Entertainment', 'publisher' => 'Unknown Worlds Entertainment']],
            'portal-2' => ['long_description' => "Portal 2 returns to Aperture Science, a vast testing facility built around puzzles that can be solved by creating linked portals on suitable surfaces. You navigate its chambers with help from the facility’s artificial intelligence, while a second voice complicates the escape plan.\n\nLater areas open up new ways to use momentum, light bridges, and gels alongside the portal device. The single-player campaign is joined by a separate cooperative campaign designed for two players and its own set of puzzles.", 'metadata' => ['developer' => 'Valve', 'publisher' => 'Valve']],
            'doom-eternal' => [
                'long_description' => "DOOM Eternal is a fast-paced first-person shooter about the Doom Slayer’s campaign against an invasion from Hell. Its combat arenas encourage constant movement and aggressive engagement, with different enemies demanding different weapons and tactics.\n\nThe Slayer’s arsenal includes firearms, a chainsaw for close-range resource recovery, and equipment that can stagger or control groups of enemies. Between battles, exploration reveals upgrade items and optional challenges, while the campaign expands the conflict across multiple locations.",
                'system_requirements' => [
